// RC4, the stream cipher from 1987 that is now a cautionary tale.
//
// It is here for interoperability and nothing else: WEP, WPA-TKIP, older TLS
// suites, Kerberos' RC4-HMAC and a long tail of file formats still carry it, and
// a library that cannot read them is a library that cannot talk to them.
//
// Do not reach for it. RC4's keystream is measurably biased — the second byte is
// zero twice as often as it should be, and long keystreams correlate with keys —
// and RFC 7465 forbids it in TLS for that reason. Its biases are a property of
// the algorithm, not of any implementation, so nothing here can be tuned to fix
// them.
import {
  "moonbitstack/mooncrypt/spec",
}

import {
  "moonbitstack/moonbase/base16",
  "moonbitlang/core/encoding/utf8",
} for "test"
